      "path": "src/ui/screens/DayCard.tsx",
      "content": "Handle the new completion variant's disclosures as well as its label. When Settle Later and acknowledged unavailable marks both apply, the coordinator now returns `CompleteWithSettlementToRecord` with `unavailable`, but the disclosure below still renders only for `CompleteWithUnavailableMarks`. The day therefore shows plain “Complete” and silently drops the instruments, trades, and uncalculated families that were previously disclosed. Render the nested `unavailable` data for this variant too, and identify the trades whose settlement remains to record.",
      "existing_code": "const COMPLETION_TEXT = { Incomplete: 'Incomplete', Complete: 'Complete', CompleteWithUnavailableMarks: 'Complete with Unavailable Marks', CompleteWithSettlementToRecord: 'Complete' } as const;",
      "start_line": 15,
      "end_line": 15,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/coordinators/daily-review/daily-review.ts",
      "content": "Use the expiration's trading session rather than requiring a replay session on the literal expiration date. Market Data explicitly supports non-session expirations: `calendarSettlementTime` resolves a weekend/holiday expiration to the preceding session's close. Replay contains trading sessions only, so a Saturday expiration will never match here, and `expirationStanding` reports `MarkMissing` even when Friday's underlying mark is available. Resolve the same session used for settlement (or select the last replay session at/before expiration), and add a non-session-expiration test.",
      "existing_code": "    const underlyingMark = replay?.sessions.find(({ date }) =\u003e date === dueContract?.expiration)?.marks.find(({ instrument }) =\u003e instrument.kind === 'Stock' \u0026\u0026 instrument.symbol === dueContract?.symbol)?.resolution;",
      "start_line": 913,
      "end_line": 913,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    }
  ],
